      "tier": "official_act",
      "text": "Votes to keep in place the existing rules, in which the national minimum wage is about 24 percent of the median full-time wage, with higher minimums set by about 60 percent of regional governments, collective agreements cover about 11 percent of employees, and an employer may dismiss most employees at any time without a stated reason, notice, or severance.",
